AUDIO_DSP is a mixed-license collection. There is no single license covering
every file. The applicable license is determined by the file header and the
boundaries below.

1. Most top-level aud_*.c and aud_*.h modules are C ports derived from the
   permissive DaisySP collection and retain the MIT license notices.

2. The following top-level module pairs are derived from DaisySP-LGPL and are
   licensed under LGPL-2.1-only, not MIT: aud_allpass, aud_balance,
   aud_bitcrush, aud_blosc, aud_comb, aud_compressor, aud_fold, aud_jitter,
   aud_line, aud_mode, aud_moogladder, aud_nlfilt, aud_pluck, aud_polypluck,
   aud_port, aud_reverbsc, and aud_tone. Their .c and .h files carry SPDX
   identifiers. Default MCU and MPU builds omit these objects; explicitly
   enabling them creates a mixed LGPL static library and requires compliance
   with the LGPL, including relinking obligations for distributed firmware.

3. Mutable Instruments STM32 algorithm sources under
   eurorack_algorithms/vendor/{braids,clouds,elements,frames,marbles,peaks,
   plaits,rings,stages,streams,tides,tides2,warps,yarns,stmlib,
   stm_audio_bootloader} are distributed
   under the MIT License unless an individual file says otherwise. The C ABI
   wrappers and examples for these modules are also distributed under MIT.

4. Branches, Edges, Grids, their AVR compatibility support, and their C ABI
   wrappers are distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later. Linking these components
   into firmware makes the resulting combined work subject to the GPL terms.
   Applications that cannot satisfy GPL distribution requirements must omit
   these three modules and their objects.

5. Original platform code under mcu/, mpu/, fpga/, and docs/ is distributed
   under the MIT License unless a file says otherwise.

6. Mutable Instruments hardware design files were not copied into this
   repository. The upstream hardware license therefore does not apply to the
   files distributed here.

Full standard license texts are in LICENSES/MIT.txt,
LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-only.txt, and LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt. Copyright and
SPDX notices in source files must be kept.

Mutable Instruments and individual module names may be trademarks of their
respective owners. This is an independent software port, not an official
Mutable Instruments product.
